   194	```markdown
   195	## Output Contract
   196	
   197	<!-- Adapted from ayghri/i-have-adhd (MIT) — condensed and adapted for jstack -->
   198	
   199	Scope: **conversational and status output only.** Artifacts — specs, plans,
   200	docs, commit messages, code comments, review reports — follow their owning
   201	skill's fidelity requirements, not this contract.
   202	
   203	1. Lead with the verdict or action. No warm-up context before the point.
   204	2. Number multi-step work. Keep lists to 5 items or fewer.
   205	3. When a turn advances multi-step work, end with 1-2 lines: current position →
   206	   next step. Include the Linear issue ID when the work is linked to one. Skip
   207	   this on short Q&A turns.
   208	4. Suppress tangents — unrequested side topics get one line at most.
   209	5. Give effort sizing (S/M/L) and the next checkpoint instead of time estimates.
   210	6. On errors and failures: calm, factual tone. No repeated apologies.
   211	7. No closing filler — no "hope this helps," no pleasantries.
   212	
   213	Exceptions override rules: when the user asks for explanation, when ambiguity
   214	needs a clarifying question, and when a destructive action needs confirmation.
   215	```
